VALUES ('authority-5d46078c6a66c2ac24c4a570', 'Cornell University College of Veterinary Medicine — Canine Health Center', 'https://www.vet.cornell.edu/departments-centers-and-institutes/riney-canine-health-center/canine-health-information/brushing-your-dogs-teeth', 'veterinary_university', 96, 'en', 'Brushing your dog''s teeth', 'dog', '["口・歯","予防・通院"]', 'Brushing your dog''s teeth
Home dental care
There is much that can be done at home to help reduce the incidence of dental disease. Brushing your dog’s teeth is the most effective method of home care for preventing dental disease. In this video, Riney Canine Health Center extension veterinarian Brian Collins, D.V.M. ’94, and his dog Speck, demonstrate how to brush your dog''s teeth.
More on dental care for your canine companion:
Dental disease and home dental care
Dental sprays
Periodontal disease
Risks from a fractured tooth', '2026-08-11T05:44:37.245Z', 1, '2026-08-11T05:44:37.245Z', '2026-08-11T05:44:37.245Z')
