VALUES ('authority-106ab1181936caf53c0b741a', 'Cornell University College of Veterinary Medicine — Feline Health Center', 'https://www.vet.cornell.edu/departments-centers-and-institutes/cornell-feline-health-center/health-information/feline-health-topics/cornell-veterinary-experts-address-feline-nutrition', 'veterinary_university', 96, 'en', 'Cornell Veterinary Experts Address Feline Nutrition', 'cat', '["食事","耳","予防・通院"]', 'Cornell Veterinary Experts Address Feline Nutrition
A balanced, healthy diet is a key component to promoting wellness and in helping treat disease in your cat. How can nutrition play a role in a cat’s health and wellness? Do cats need vitamins and supplements in their food? Are raw food diets safe? Watch the video below as Cornell trained veterinary experts discuss the many different aspects of feline nutrition.
Purrfect Nutrition to keep your cat "feline" good!
Obesity is recognized as a serious health concern among Americans today, putting more and more of us at risk for chronic illnesses and earlier mortality. Unfortunately, the unhealthy eating habits of many Americans often extend to their pets as well. A Cornell College of Veterinary Medicine follow-up to a 2,000-plus cat feline obesity study showed several serious effects.', '2026-08-11T05:44:37.245Z', 1, '2026-08-11T05:44:37.245Z', '2026-08-11T05:44:37.245Z')
