The outlook for recovery is usually good, depending on the injury and the success of the surgery. Follow-up care includes x-rays and veterinary checkups to assess how the fracture is healing. Removal of internal implants like bone plates or screws is not necessary unless complications such as stress protection, infection, and soft-tissue irritation develop.
