VALUES ('authority-6e683fb7e1df066ab6096e9f', 'MSD/Merck Veterinary Manual — Dog Owners', 'https://www.merckvetmanual.com/dog-owners/digestive-disorders-of-dogs/dental-disorders-of-dogs', 'peer_reviewed_veterinary_manual', 92, 'en', 'Dental Disorders of Dogs', 'dog', '["食事","目・涙","耳","口・歯","行動・しつけ","予防・通院","高齢","運動器","腫瘍"]', 'PET OWNER VERSION
Dental Disorders of Dogs
Full Review: May 2018 By Alexander M. Reiter , Dipl. Tzt., DEVDC, DAVDC , Department of Clinical Sciences & Advanced Medicine, School of Veterinary
Medicine, University of Pennsylvania Last updated: Oct 2025
v3202061
View the Professional Version
Gum Disease |
Endodontic Disease |
Developmental Abnormalities |
Trauma to the Face and Jaw |
Tooth Decay (Cavities) |
For More Information |
Multimedia |
Many of the dental disorders of dogs are similar to those found in people. Proper dental care, including preventive methods like tooth brushing, can help keep your dog’s teeth and gums healthy.
Table
Dental Terms
Table
