VALUES ('authority-e988e1303fb2cba53bd85f3a', 'MSD/Merck Veterinary Manual — Dog Owners', 'https://www.merckvetmanual.com/dog-owners/bone-joint-and-muscle-disorders-of-dogs/introduction-to-bone-joint-and-muscle-disorders-of-dogs', 'peer_reviewed_veterinary_manual', 92, 'en', 'Introduction to Bone, Joint, and Muscle Disorders of Dogs', 'dog', '["皮膚・被毛","予防・通院","運動器"]', 'PET OWNER VERSION
Introduction to Bone, Joint, and Muscle Disorders of Dogs
Full Review: Mar 2018 By Stephen B. Adams , DVM, DACVS , Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, College of Veterinary Medicine,
Purdue University Last updated: Sept 2024
v3205097
The musculoskeletal system includes the bones, cartilage, muscles, ligaments, joints, tendons, and other connective tissue. It supports the body, permits movement, and protects the vital organs. Because many other body systems (including the nervous system, blood vessels, and skin) are interrelated, disorders of one of these systems may also affect the musculoskeletal system.
